# graphify: paths kept out of the knowledge graph.
# graphify reads this file, not .gitignore, so generated and local-only files
# are listed here as well. Folders whose names start with a dot (.claude/ and
# its worktrees, .github/, .git/) are always skipped.

# graphify's own output. graphify-out/memory/ stays in on purpose: answers
# saved with `graphify save-result` are fed back into the graph.
graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
graphify-out/graph.html
graphify-out/wiki/
graphify-out/obsidian/

# Claude instructions: loaded into every Claude session already, and today it
# holds only the graphify rules
CLAUDE.md

# Version history and dated review reports. Most findings in reports/ are
# already fixed, and IDs such as H-01 repeat across reports, so extracting them
# would put stale claims in the graph with no reliable link to code.
# Delete these two lines to include them (about 110k words of LLM extraction).
CHANGELOG.md
reports/

# Documentation website: its own build, with pages that restate README sections
site/

# Throwaway probes. Under the D:\SCRIPTS_PATH convention a script named
# *temporal* is temporary; these reproduced the scan pilot failures.
# tests/temporal_* are the real tests for php/Temporal*.php and stay in.
tools/temporal_*
fixh4_temporal.js

# Slide deck and field-training exports: large HTML, not module documentation
docs/user-guide-deck.html
docs/Participant_Identification_and_REDCAP_Data_Validation*.html

# Flier and stray local PDFs
*.pdf
